 "title": "Haskell: The Craft of Functional Programming (3rd edition)",
 "byline": "Simon Thompson \u00b7 Addison-Wesley 2011; free CC BY-NC-ND PDF, 2023",
 "note": "PDF page = printed page + 19. This free 2023 PDF is still the current version; the author plans a revised interactive online edition. Exercises and the appendices (imperative vs. functional, glossary, operators, practicalities, GHCi errors, project ideas) are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "A first course in functional programming with Haskell that stresses the craft of designing, testing and reasoning about programs rather than language features. Using a running Pictures example and other case studies, it moves from basic types, definitions and recursion through tuples, lists and list comprehensions, I/O with a rock\u2013paper\u2013scissors game, and proof by induction, to higher-order functions and patterns of computation, type classes and type inference, algebraic and abstract data types (Huffman codes, queues, search trees, sets, graphs), lazy and infinite structures with a parsing case study, monads, domain-specific languages including QuickCheck generators, and time and space behaviour."
}